<id/doc/doc_guarana_bread/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Guarana Bread"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a name in Brazil for cakes made from the seeds of the *Paullinia sorbilis*, and used like cocoa for making a beverage; it contains a bitter principle, identical with caffeine. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 194]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_guarana_bread" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Guarana Bread"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0122 (Drugs Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 194."@en ;
